<title>UK: FORECAST-Expert predictions for UK election - table.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Expert predictions for UK election - table.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are results of a Reuters survey of predictions by 20 leading experts in voting behaviour of the outcome of a British general election which must take place by May 1997.</p>
<p>Opinions were canvassed on Friday September 27 and Monday September 30.</p>
<p> 1				     Who will win? With what majority? Election date?</p>
<p> John Benyon, University of Leicester Labour		23		   May</p>
<p> David Carlton, Univ of Warwick	 Conservative	 9		  April</p>
<p> Neil Carter, Univ of York		Labour		11		   May</p>
<p> Ivor Crewe, Univ of Essex		Labour		61		   May</p>
